{
  "_comment": "Hostile StepInput values shared by every port. Each 'reject' entry is one field set to one JSON value with the other fields at 0; the port must refuse it (exception, error return, decode error or trap) and must never account it. class=negative applies to every port. class=non_integer applies to ports whose StepInput accepts untyped values (Python, Node, PHP, Ruby); statically typed ports (Go, Rust, Java, C#, Swift) satisfy it by refusing to decode the value into their integer field, and their runners report it as such. 'accept' entries must be handled without overflow, NaN or a crash, under default (1.x) config. Pressure after a release is 0.0 and post_release_lock leaves the engine locked.",
  "version": "1.0",
  "reject": [
    {
      "name": "tokens_negative_one",
      "field": "tokens",
      "value": -1,
      "class": "negative"
    },
    {
